SURVIVAL PROTOCOL

Night Operation's run (coop nightop), the challenges (coop challenge,
which run on the same code) and the friend's revive adapt code from Survival
Protocol by SchizoEffective (Nexus Mods, Stellar Blade mod 4009,
https://www.nexusmods.com/stellarblade/mods/4009). The challenge list
follows Survival Protocol's graded stages: five difficulty stages picked
from a list before a fight.

SchizoEffective gave permission to use this code in Stellar Blade Online on
2026-10-20, and agreed on Discord on 2026-11-14 to the project's move from
GPL-3.0 to a license that bans AyakaMods. The adapted code is licensed here
under the SBO License, version 1.0 or any later version that the Licensor
publishes, with the additional permission above. The adapted functions are
marked in mod/StellarCoop/Scripts/online/modes/nightop/run.lua,
online/modes/nightop/waves.lua and core/unreal.lua. Stellar Blade Online
contains no file from Survival Protocol.

EVE ON WHEELS

The bike's riding model and its lean adapt code from Eve On Wheels 1.2.1 by
dCharisma1 (Nexus Mods, Stellar Blade mod 4165,
https://www.nexusmods.com/stellarblade/mods/4165), who is credited as the
author of that code.

dCharisma1 gave his written consent on 2026-11-16 to the use of his Eve On
Wheels code in Stellar Blade Online under the SBO License, version 1.0 or
any later version that the Licensor publishes. The adapted code is licensed
here under those terms. The adapted functions are marked in
mod/StellarCoop/Scripts/vehicles/bike/model.lua and vehicles/bike/ride.lua.
Stellar Blade Online contains no file from Eve On Wheels: none of its
assets, sounds or animations.

EVE HOVERBIKE

The bike's riding rig (bike_pose=rig) adapts the puppet ride of Eve
Hoverbike by kwisatz (GitHub sarojratul): a hidden copy that plays the
riding pose while EVE's body and outfit parts copy its bones.

kwisatz gave his written permission on 2026-11-20 to adapt that code into
Stellar Blade Online under the SBO License, version 1.0 or any later
version that the Licensor publishes, in his comment on pull request 11:
https://github.com/MotherSphere/stellar-blade-coop/pull/11#issuecomment-7047471384
The adapted code is licensed here under those terms. It is
mod/StellarCoop/Scripts/vehicles/bike/rig.lua (its header says so) and the
rig way in vehicles/bike/ride.lua. Stellar Blade Online contains no file
from Eve Hoverbike.

GUN MODE

Gun mode's rifle stance and laser sight
(mod/StellarCoop/Scripts/fight/gunmode/stance.lua and
fight/gunmode/laser.lua) are luke77's RifleStance, which Lucas (luke77)
contributed to this project in the commit "feat: add standing rifle stance
and aiming laser". Gun mode around them is by SchizoEffective.

Stellar Blade Online ships no animation file. Gun mode's rifle layer
needs an optional pak, zNGMSpike_P, which holds the layer (ABP_NGM_Spike)
and the rifle clips it plays. The pak is not part of Stellar Blade
Online. tools/gunmode/rebuild/ngm_spike_build_a4.py makes it on the
player's own PC from an Unreal project that is not in this repository.
This repository does not record where those rifle clips come from. The
scripts in tools/gunmode/blender/ made an earlier standing rifle set from
Mixamo's "Rifle 8-Way Locomotion Pack" (Adobe, under Mixamo's terms) and
from Stellar Blade's own animations, both read on the player's own PC.
Neither is in this repository.

THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

A third-party component keeps its own license, and the SBO License grants
nothing in it. The repository holds no third-party library source. These
parts come close:

- The DLL is built with clang-cl against the Microsoft C and C++ runtime,
  linked statically. That runtime is Microsoft's and comes under the terms
  of the build tools that provided it.
- The native part calls the Steamworks API in the game's own
  steam_api64.dll. Stellar Blade Online ships no Steamworks file. Steamworks
  is Valve's.
- UE4SS, which loads the mod, is installed by the player. The release zip
  does not contain it.

UE4SS FILES FOR STELLAR BLADE

ue4ss/builds/ holds the files that UE4SS v4.0.0 needs to run on a given
Stellar Blade build, one folder per build. The release zip does not contain
them.

GNatives.lua and GUObjectArray.lua in ue4ss/builds/6ad8eff1-15fa3000/ come
from Rev-OG-UwU's SB-UE4SS (https://github.com/Rev-OG-UwU/SB-UE4SS, commit
a63c3f8ecfc51c679082c30805d8af5c3514ba9a). They first appear in Chrisr0's
RE-UE4SS (https://github.com/Chrisr0/RE-UE4SS, commit
e6e59de93656ed3caf242233a0b6f63e073ba3df, June 2025), the repository that
Rev-OG-UwU's fork names as its base. The header of each file says what was
changed here.

Two parts of that fork are left out. Its backup_saves() copies the player's
save at every start. Stellar Blade Online never touches the player's own
saves. FText_Constructor.lua is not shipped: it is a known cause of
games that do not start. UE4SS v4.0.0 does not read it.

